      "id": "berklee-music-theory-book-1-p0068",
      "source_en": "Lesson 29. The Descending Melodic Minor Scale\n\nMelodic minor scales descend in two different ways. The traditional melodic minor scale descends with scale degrees 6 and 7 lowered by a half step, reverting back to the natural minor form. C Natural Minor\n\nDo Re Me Fa Sol Le Te Do Do Te Le Sol Fa Me Re Do\n\nC Traditional Melodic Minor\n\n1 2 b3 4 5 n6 n7 8 8 b7 b6 5 4 b3 2 1 Do Re Me Fa Sol La Ti Do Do Te Le Sol Fa Me Re Do\n\nThe real melodic minor descends just as it ascends, with scale degrees 6 and 7 raised. C Natural Minor\n\nDo Re Me Fa Sol Le Te Do Do Te Le Sol Fa Me Re Do\n\nC Real Melodic Minor\n\n1 2 b3 4 5 n6 n7 8 8 n7 n6 5 4 b3 2 1 Do Re Me Fa Sol La Ti Do Do Ti La Sol Fa Me Re Do",
